{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CejGkwbPr7TVW5WTixk9y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm waiting on the full suite. Meanwhile, here's where WI-591 stands.\n\n**Verdict: the WI-584 close STANDS, with one finding.**\n\nWhat I verified by driving the shipped code (not reading the record):\n- Ruling (a) is genuinely built — `refresh_refusal` scopes to `_authorised_registries`, the same function `copy_live` writes from.\n- The deliberately-unscoped arm (empty write set → judged globally) is present and tested.\n- **The named acceptance re-drives at this tip**: `refresh_refusal('.', {llr: 'the sitting'})` → `''`; the bare call still refuses.\n- Six tests exist and are the six claimed; the non-vacuity case is real.\n- `check_complexity` → `OK - 199 row(s) over 15, unchanged from baseline` (no bump taken, as claimed).\n- No spine file in the WI-584 commit range → \"no approval brief owed\" holds.\n\n**The finding.** WI-584's Context called the refusal header (`\"…nothing in this working tree authorises it\"`) false and said it was worth correcting \"under either reading\"; its Deliverable claims the new text went **in place of** it. It did not — it went *after* it. Driven live, the scoped arm now emits both sentences in sequence, contradicting itself:\n\n```\n… and nothing in this working tree authorises it:\n  docs/requirements/system-requirements.toml SR-006: Title\nThis act DOES authorise system-requirements.toml; …\n```\n\n`_refusal_text` branches its middle line on `scope` but leaves the opening line constant, so the header is true only on the arm where `scope` is empty — false on exactly the arm the ruling built. Existing tests pass because none of them reads the first line.\n\nA `quick`-tier successor is drafted under `## Dispositions`. I also recorded one non-finding (the unscoped arm's one-flag mute is defensible, not a defect) and one immaterial 3-vs-4 count discrepancy inside WI-584's own record.\n\nFindings are committed at `f6e06279`; the Deliverable text is staged in the working tree and lands with the close commit (R-A rejects a filled Deliverable while the row is still `active`)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":627,"cache_read_input_tokens":88034,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":627},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c3dd299e-18fb-44bd-9054-e14977d24ac0","uuid":"add20c91-6547-4ae5-a59b-7c2cba75bbf8","request_id":"req_011CejGkv1trzmHJGRnWi2EH"}
